A||||11||DavidHenshaw||Door  window removal||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||03-02-2001||07:47 PM||||Was trying to replace outer dew wipe on drivers side in my 86 GT with power windows. All went fine until I found one of the screws which sits behind the glass was totally rusted and can't be turned out. <P>Hope I'm wrong but looks like the only solution is to remove the glass and drill the screw. Can the window be lowered? If that's not possible what is the procedure to remove the window.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||03-02-2001||08:05 PM||||I have not faced this problem (Thank God!) but you might try grabbing the screw head with a small pair of offset pliers (ChannelLocks).  Or you could cut off the screw head with a hacksaw blade and ignore it.  I'm guessing that you would bend the door structure if you try to back-out the screw with a chisel.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||03-02-2001||08:25 PM||||Thanks MrPBody, but the problem is clearance or lack thereof. There just isn't more than 1/2 inch between the glass and the dew wipe rail. BTW what did you do with Sherman's body?<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||03-02-2001||08:42 PM||||When I replaced the wipes on a friend's GT, I just drilled out the rivits holding the glass in and removed the window. The rivits are 25-50 cents at a glass shop. Made the job a little easier. Be warned- these rivits take a large gun!||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||03-02-2001||09:00 PM||||I didn't say it would be easy.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I thought I was going to strip a screw when I replaced my dew wipes, but I dodged <I>that</I> bullet.<P>I haven't tried to remove a window.  Maybe it's the way to go.<P>Sherman?  Haven't seen him for years.  The Wayback Machine returned without him.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||03-02-2001||09:14 PM||||Cooter, do we need any more info on the rivet<BR>gun (size),(type)? I need to replace the windows in the toy. I have a good set in one of my parts cars and I was just waiting on the dew wipes to get here before I jump into it. Is there another info I need??. Any difference in power and non-power windows??<P>Thanks<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000006||Cooter||03-02-2001||09:45 PM||||I 'think' that they are 1/4 inch body, long shaft "butterfly" rivits. We have a "big-daddy" rivit gun at the shop/ It is about the size of a large set of bolt cutters. The OEM rivits have a steel center and aluminum body, so it is much easier to center punch the center out and then drill the head off. Any glass shop will have them, but getting them to sell you some might be a different story.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||03-02-2001||10:51 PM||||You can get the Large Hand Riveter from Harbor Freight for about $16 US.  It handles up to 1/4" rivets and comes with 25 each of 4 size rivets.<P>Cooter,<P>Did you have to remove the door skin to drill out the rivets and remove the glass or did you do it from the inside?<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||03-03-2001||02:06 AM||||We did it from the inside. There are 4 rivits per glass- 2 on the window track and 2 travel stops at each end of the glass.||||reg||1
Z||000009||gabriel||03-03-2001||07:57 AM||||I did it from the inside without using rivets.<P>  You drill out the 4 rivets as outlined above, then head to the hardware or Auto store for 4 1" bolts & nuts.  You might be able to use 1 1/4" , but 1" is what I used.<P>  Assemble the components finger tight outside the door, then hot melt the nuts on to the back of the plastic things.<P>  Use loctite on the bolts.  It's a little tricky to get all the bolts in, but it can be done.    Cost me about five bucks.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfixit58||03-03-2001||09:07 AM||||Whoa! TIME OUT -- TIME OUT!!<P>YOU DON"T HAVE TO DRILL OUT ANYTHING!<P>To get to the two hidden screws, just unbolt the slider tracks from the front and back of the door. You can then just grab the window and push it forward and backwards out of your way. When you put it back together, just put the screws back into the same location (it will be obvious where the came from).<P>The first side will be a learning experience but the second side will be muh quicker. I changed out both sides in my car in just under an hour. That includes removing and re-installing the door panels. It was only the second car I've done.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000011||gabriel||03-03-2001||12:30 PM||||&gt;Whoa! TIME OUT -- TIME OUT!!<P> Guess I got ahead of myself. - hehe. I should have added that I wasn't changing my dew wipes, I was replacing the entire window, & if that could be done w/o drilling, I'd sure have been happy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>     -thanks||||reg||1
